int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(1); // exit with exit code 1
}

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(2); // exit with exit code 2
}
```

In this example, the program will exit with exit code 1 if it encounters an error, and exit with exit code 2 if it encounters a success.

